  "summaries": [
    {
      "id": 21488,
      "category": "team",
      "content": "Summary:\njust on intercepting and going through the request i made from ort-admin.pingone.com . i found that the google map api key was leaking through get request . i was able to validate that the leaked key was a valid one\n\nSteps To Reproduce:\n1.login to account\n\ngoto setup tab > ping iD > device pairing\ngoto add an ip and enter an ip\nclick save and intercept the request\nhave a look to the GET request and see the google map api key was leaked through request\nleaked key is █████\n\n███\n\ni was able to validate thatt this key was a valid one by using an endpoint that validate the key\n\nhttps://maps.googleapis.com/maps/api/staticmap?center=40.714728,-73.998672&zoom=12&size=2500x2000&maptype=roadmap&key=XXXXX\n\nthis shows that this is a valid key\n\nImpact\nany persons can use this api key for their own use",
